# Miro-to-Markdown Subproject - Cursor Rules

## Subproject Context
This subproject implements:
1. A local Backcasting MCP server (read/write Markdown nodes)
2. Miro → Markdown conversion pipeline

## Key Specifications
- MCP interface: `docs/backcasting-mcp-spec.md`
- Node format: `docs/backcasting-map-spec.md`
- Product vision: `docs/prod-vision.md`

## Technical Stack (Target)
- Python 3.11+
- `python-frontmatter` for Markdown parsing
- MCP SDK or custom JSON-RPC for MCP tools
- Miro REST API or Miro MCP (TBD after spike)

## Implementation Guidelines
- Keep the MCP server simple; run locally without heavy infrastructure
- Prefer plain files + conventions over database
- All MCP tool responses follow HATEOAS pattern with `_links`
- Preserve existing node IDs when updating; generate new IDs only for new nodes

## Directory Structure (Target)
```
miro-to-markdown/
├── docs/           # Specifications
├── src/
│   ├── mcp_server/ # Backcasting MCP server
│   └── miro_client/# Miro API integration
├── tests/
└── README.md
```

## Current Phase
Phase 1: Backcasting MCP Server (Local Read/Write)
- Focus on `get_template`, `get_node`, `write_node` first
- Chain traversal (`get_chain_from_root`) in Phase 2




